  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday morning through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 158 PM EST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nCalm and pleasant fall weather is expected through the long term \nforecast as high pressure settles in across much of the southeast. \nExpect highs in the upper 60s and low 70s during the day with \novernight lows falling into the 40s and 30s by the end of the \nweekend. While widespread freezing/ frost is not expected, some \nareas of higher elevations could come close to hazardous for \nsensitive plants.\n\nChance of rain through the long term is as scientifically as low as \nit can go. RH values falling into the 30 and 40% range during the \nafternoon are the tell-tale signs that conditions will remain dry \nand precipitation will be unlikely.",
